# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Computer Operator generated evidence — defense in depth
#
# NOTHING listed here is produced inside the repo today. Every one of these lives outside it
# (C:\Aroma\ComputerOperator-Evidence, C:\Aroma\Commissioning-Reports, C:\AromaOperator-Probe).
# These rules exist so that if an output path is ever mistyped or a probe is ever run with the
# repo as its working directory, the artefact cannot be committed by accident. They protect
# against a future mistake, not a present leak.
#
# ── READ THIS IF GIT IS REFUSING TO ADD YOUR FILE ──────────────────────────
# Three of these are REPO-WIDE by filename, not confined to a directory:
#     **/*.lnk        **/stage3-*.json        **/*-baseline*.xml
# So a LEGITIMATE future file matching one of those names will silently fail to be added, and
# `git add` will say nothing useful. That is the exact silent-failure shape this project keeps
# getting bitten by, so it is written down here rather than left to be rediscovered.
#   . to see whether a rule is the reason:   git check-ignore -v <path>
#   . to commit a legitimate file anyway:    git add -f <path>
# If you find yourself using -f more than once for the same kind of file, narrow the rule
# instead — an override used routinely is a rule that is wrong.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# the evidence root: probe results, captures, manifests, ACL baselines, audit markers
**/ComputerOperator-Evidence/
# the readable copies produced by launcher 3 (every round, with SHA-256 index)
**/Commissioning-Reports/
# the staged probe scripts and their output, behind the Gate B DENY boundary
**/AromaOperator-Probe/
# fail-safe stop reports written by any commissioning launcher — machine state, by design
**/FAILED-*.json
**/FAILED-*.txt
# Part A/B harness output: run manifest, results, STARTED/COMPLETED markers, UIA dumps
**/stage3-*.json
# sentinel and owner-reference captures — screen contents of a live session
**/stage3-*.png
# observer run records and their captures/UIA text
**/obs-*.json
**/obs-*.png
**/obs-*.txt
# scheduled-task baselines exported before a change (observer task, gate task)
**/*-baseline*.xml
# the probe-directory ACL captured before Gate B was applied
**/probedir-acl-pre-*.txt
# desktop shortcuts are generated per machine by the bootstrap/installer, never source
**/*.lnk
